How You Publish Moving Forward:
Whenever you have a new whitepaper or case study:
Write the article and save it as journal/your-slug-title.html.
Open journal-posts.json and paste your new object at the top:
JSON
{
  "id": "post-4",
  "slug": "journal/your-slug-title.html",
  "title": "Title of Your New Field Brief",
  "category": "architectural",
  "categoryLabel": "Architectural Cinema",
  "date": "October 2026",
  "readTime": "6 min read",
  "excerpt": "A short 2-sentence summary of the takeaway.",
  "image": "https://your-image-url.jpg",
  "imageAlt": "Description of image",
  "featured": true
}
Set "featured": true if you want it to command the hero banner at the top (and set the previous one to false).
Save journal-posts.json, commit it, and the entire journal renders automatically with complete responsive styling, instant category filters, and zero layout bugs.
